   "name": "Exelixis Inc"
  },
  "created_at": "2026-06-02T13:05:51.662667Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-06-15T13:05:59.953687Z",
  "ticker": "EXEL",
  "drug_name": "CABOMETYX",
  "drug_indication": "Previously Treated Advanced Neuroendocrine Tumors",
  "airtable_id": 7987,
  "stage": "Phase 3",
  "catalyst_date": "2026-05-29",
  "catalyst_source": "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260529816966/en/Exelixis-Announces-Results-from-Subgroup-Analysis-of-Phase-3-CABINET-Pivotal-Trial-Evaluating-CABOMETYX-cabozantinib-in-Non-Functional-and-Functional-Neuroendocrine-Tumors-at-ASCO-2026",
  "catalyst_text": "Presented positive phase 3 subgroup data improving PFS",
  "detailed_catalyst_text": "Reported subgroup analysis results from the phase 3 CABINET trial in previously treated advanced neuroendocrine tumors, showing significant progression-free survival benefits versus placebo in both non-functional and functional subgroups. Presented at ASCO 2026, the findings support efficacy across functional status and reinforce clinical utility in this population.",
  "catalyst_text_evidence": "\"Exelixis, Inc. (NASDAQ:EXEL) today announced results from a subgroup analysis of the phase 3 CABINET pivotal trial, which showed that CABOMETYX\u00ae (cabozantinib) provided significant improvements in progression-free survival (PFS) versus placebo in patients with previously treated advanced neuroendocrine tumors (NET) regardless of functional status.\" \"These data will be presented at the 2026 American Society of Clinical Oncology (ASCO) Annual Meeting to be held from 2026-05-29 \u2013 2026-06-02 in Chicago.\" \"These subgroup results presented today at ASCO 2026 show cabozantinib demonstrated improvements in PFS regardless of functional status.\" \"In patients with non-functional NET, the hazard ratio (HR) was 0.26 (95% confidence interval [CI]: 0.17\u20130.41; p<0.001); median PFS was 9.4 months with cabozantinib (95% CI: 8.5\u201313.8) versus 3.1 months with placebo (95% CI: 2.9\u20135.7). In patients with functional NET, the HR was 0.40 (95% CI: 0.20\u20130.82; p=0.012); median PFS was 12.7 months (95% CI: 8.4\u201317.9) with cabozantinib versus 5.4 months with placebo (95% CI: 3.7\u2013not estimable).\"",
  "news_published_at": "2026-06-02T00:00:00Z",
  "open_price_gap_percent": "0.00773",
  "intra_day_price_change_percent": "-0.01160"
 },
